Here's my Arduino sketch that blinks an LED with millis() and prints to Serial. Port it to bare-metal AVR C for the Uno, no Arduino core at all.

void setup(){ pinMode(13, OUTPUT); Serial.begin(9600); }
void loop(){ static unsigned long t; if (millis()-t >= 500){ t = millis(); digitalWrite(13, !digitalRead(13)); Serial.println("tick"); } }
